•fauthorxApub:sha2-256:ks7g2ycpdnhjdtsn3sfoiqoh2tazwtiwr2emxut3ugourttnnbkadbodyßeclassharchivalgcontentxqpubkit 0.21.0 was released on 2026-10-30 from commit ff9f36e08b38ee8f34c0061d11c4bc37c8cb1723 with these changes.ddata¢gcolumnsÇ°dnamehcategory°dnamefchangedrowsÇÇgchangedyÍA Rust repository's pull requests no longer run msrv, fuzz and cross on every push: pubkit sync writes queue.yml, which the merge queue runs (merge_group) with every pull request job and those three besides, so nothing merges before they pass, and pr.yml runs on pull_request alone. The ci block's events gain queue, on by default; where the queue would run nothing a pull request does not (Node, Python and service repositories by default) there is no queue.yml and pr.yml runs on merge_group as before, and a repository without a merge queue leaves queue out so its pull requests run the heavy jobs. main.yml's tested asks for the queue's workflow by name and skips only the jobs the queue ran; queue.yml carries the release and site checks tooÇgchangedyNew packages' CI, and pubkit's own, call pubrel 0.6.1's release workflow, pinned by its tag's commit, and so pass it the release app's RELEASE_APP_ID and RELEASE_APP_KEY, which pubrel 0.6.1 is the first to take: pubrel tag then tags with the app the Sustenaut tag ruleset lets throughgdependsÅxApub:sha2-256:2akz6i5benvzci3et4qtyebzbojzjzu4f5ubtgecxoytnhce3gmqhevidenceÅ§dkindhexternalcreffpubkithrevisionx(ff9f36e08b38ee8f34c0061d11c4bc37c8cb1723drolefsourcedlangbenescope¢jconditionsÄfdomainx'the published release v0.21.0 of pubkitgcreatedt2026-10-30T00:00:00Zcpuba1dtypekclaim.prose